      ":question/id": "afa20041-c2f3-52b2-aa20-c3354dca4f1a",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 6 & -1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 6 & -9 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -3 & 4 & -7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5 & -8 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry ${a}_{34}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 6 & -1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since the first row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated). \n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 6 & -9 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry ${c}_{45}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -3 & 4 & -7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5 & -8 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ are **not** in row echelon form.",
